ducks lay 16 eggs per day, so she has 16 * 7 = 112 eggs per week. She eats three for breakfast every morning, so she has 112 - 3 * 7 = 91 eggs left for baking muffins. She bakes muffins for her friends every day with four, so she has 91 / 4 = 22.75 muffins. She sells the remainder at the farmers' market daily for $2 per fresh duck egg, so she has $2 * 22.75 = $45.50 per day.
Answer:
45.50
